@startuml
title T12-WF04 — AI CRM Follow-up Agent
start
:01 | Webhook Trigger\nreceive the protected internal request from NestJS for a persisted FollowUpExecution; NestJS waits for the synchronous DeliveryResult; do not also trigger this execution through RabbitMQ.;
:02 | Code: Validate Execution Request\nvalidate execution, enrollment, step, channel and correlation IDs.;
:03 | Backend: Load Follow-up Context\nFollowUpService loads the authoritative enrollment, Lead and step before n8n dispatch.;
:04 | Backend: Check Eligibility\nNestJS validates enrollment state, active step, due time and duplicate-execution safeguards before dispatch.;
:05 | Backend: Render Message Payload\nFollowUpService resolves subjectTemplate/contentTemplate, renders recipient/subject/message and persists requestPayload before n8n dispatch; this is not an n8n node.;
:06 | HTTP Request: Backend Send Message\nPOST /api/v1/internal/communication/follow-ups/{executionId}/send with an empty body and Idempotency-Key equal to executionId.;
:07 | Backend: Claim and Deliver\nCommunicationService loads the persisted payload, claims idempotent delivery and sends through backend-configured SMTP.;
:08 | Webhook Response: Return Delivery Result\nreturn the authoritative DeliveryResult to the original FollowUpService dispatch call; do not call a separate delivery-callback endpoint.;
:09 | Backend: Persist Execution Outcome\nFollowUpService records the returned status and correlation/idempotency identity.;
if (10 | Delivery succeeded?) then (yes)
  :11 | Backend: Advance/Complete\nFollowUpService advances the step or completes the enrollment transactionally only after confirmed SENT.;
else (no)
  :12 | Backend: Handle Delivery Failure\nFollowUpService applies bounded retry for definite retryable failures or records terminal failure; UNKNOWN is never blindly resent.;
endif
note right
UC06 uses the protected NestJS-to-n8n Webhook request/response path; there is no RabbitMQ trigger or asynchronous result callback in this implementation.\nThe PR #72 export currently has six functional nodes.\nWF04 owner remains responsible for the final 12-functional-node graph and runtime acceptance.


end note
stop
@enduml
